// staff, it will need a separate number from the mid-measure slurs because it
// overlaps those slurs in MusicXML document order. However, if the cross-staff
// slur starts in the bottom staff and stops in the top staff, all three slurs
// can use the same number. None of them overlap within the MusicXML document,
// even though they all overlap each other in the musical score order. Within
// the MusicXML document, the start and stop of the top-staff slur will be
// followed by the stop and start of the cross-staff slur, followed by the start
// and stop of the bottom-staff slur.
